quran[24]{c,v,t}:
  55,17,(He is) the Lord of the two easts and the Lord of the two wests.
  55,18,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,19,"He merged the two seas, meeting each other."
  55,20,Between them is a barrier they do not transgress.
  55,21,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,22,Out of both (waters) come out pearls and coral stones.
  55,23,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,24,"(Under) His (control) are the ships floating on the sea, (appearing) like mountains."
  55,25,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,26,Every being on earth is bound to perish.
  55,27,"Your Lord (alone), full of Majesty and Honour, will remain forever."
  55,28,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,29,"Those in the heavens and the earth ask Him (only). Every day, He manifests (a new state of) Glory."
  55,30,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,31,"We will soon attend to you (for judgement), O two multitudes (of humans and jinn)!"
  55,32,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,33,"O assembly of the jinn and the humans! If you can penetrate beyond the regions of the heavens and the earth, then penetrate through (them). But you cannot penetrate through (them) without (Our) authority."
  55,34,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,35,"Flames of fire and (a cloud of) smoke will be released upon you; then, you will not be able to defend yourselves."
  55,36,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,37,(How terrible it will be) when the sky splits apart and turns rose-red like burnt oil (or tanned leather).
  55,38,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,39,"On that Day, neither humans nor the jinn will be questioned about their sins."
  55,40,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
